# PAWPLE CURSOR RULES (STRICT ENFORCEMENT)

You are building Pawple — a calm, premium, emotionally restrained pet journaling & meetup app.

Pawple is NOT a traditional social media product.

It should feel:
• warm
• calm
• breathable
• emotionally soft
• premium
• human
• pet-first
• Apple-inspired

NOT:
❌ engagement-driven
❌ loud
❌ cluttered
❌ heavily decorated
❌ utility-heavy
❌ influencer-oriented

ALWAYS follow these rules.
NEVER deviate unless explicitly instructed.

-----------------------------------------------------
🧭 DESIGN GOVERNANCE & DECISION AUTHORITY
-----------------------------------------------------

This section defines who owns Pawple decisions. It does not change any existing
product, visual-system, architecture, or implementation rule below.

FOUNDER & MANAGING DIRECTOR

Owns:
• Pawple's fundamental product vision and identity
• the pet-first philosophy and core product principles
• long-term strategic direction
• fundamental changes to product scope
• consequential decisions affecting Pawple's identity, privacy, safety, trust,
  or material user behaviour
• founder-level strategic decisions

The Founder & Managing Director does not need to approve individual visual-system
implementation details such as exact spacing values, individual corner radii,
typography sizes or weights, button geometry, component-level visual treatment,
or responsive layout details unless those choices materially change Pawple's
product identity or user behaviour.

CEO / EXECUTIVE LEADERSHIP

Owns:
• operational leadership
• translating strategic direction into execution
• coordinating functional leadership
• day-to-day company and product decisions within the established mandate
• ensuring execution remains aligned with Pawple's product principles and
  strategic direction
• escalating founder-level or materially consequential decisions to the
  Founder & Managing Director

DESIGN / UX

Owns visual-system and interaction-design execution within Pawple's established
product principles, including:
• typography system
• spacing system and visual rhythm
• component geometry and consistency
• colour application
• hierarchy
• interaction patterns
• screen composition
• responsive behaviour
• accessibility-oriented presentation

Design / UX may evaluate and select the most appropriate implementation when
existing visual rules contain conflicts without Founder & Managing Director
approval for ordinary visual-system execution.

Design / UX must preserve:
• pet-first identity
• Pawple's established warmth and personality
• Apple-inspired simplicity, clarity, restraint, hierarchy, progressive
  disclosure, and intuitive interaction
• existing product principles and scope

Design / UX must not independently change:
• product functionality or scope
• mating or matching criteria
• privacy or safety rules
• chat or other product behaviour
• major product architecture
• established Product Contract requirements

ARCHITECTURE

Owns:
• technical and data architecture
• system boundaries
• integration patterns
• database and storage architecture
• engineering approach

Architecture must respect the Product Contract and established product and
design principles.

ENGINEERING

Owns implementation of approved product, design, and architecture decisions.
Engineering must not silently change product behaviour or design principles
during implementation.

DECISION ESCALATION

A decision must return to the Founder & Managing Director when it:
• changes Pawple's fundamental identity
• changes the pet-first principle
• fundamentally changes product vision
• makes a major strategic change to product scope
• materially changes a consequential user journey
• affects privacy, safety, or trust at founder-level significance
• changes an established Product Contract requirement where such a change is
  actually authorized
• introduces a major new product mechanic with significant strategic
  implications

CEO / Executive Leadership handles ordinary operational and product decisions
within its established mandate.

A decision does not require Founder & Managing Director approval merely because
it involves:
• 20px versus 24px spacing
• an exact corner radius
• exact typography sizing
• button geometry
• component-level visual refinement
• responsive layout details

This applies only when the decision remains consistent with Pawple's established
product principles, approved product direction, scope, and Product Contract.

-----------------------------------------------------
🧠 CORE PRODUCT PHILOSOPHY
-----------------------------------------------------

Pawple should feel like:
“A quiet collection of saved pet memories.”

NOT:
❌ Instagram clone
❌ Pinterest aesthetic
❌ scrapbook craft project
❌ event management app
❌ creator platform

RULE:
Every screen should prioritize:
1. the pet/content
2. emotional warmth
3. calm composition

NOT:
the design system itself.

-----------------------------------------------------
🧠 COMPOSITION PHILOSOPHY (STRICT)
-----------------------------------------------------

Screens should feel:
• inevitable
• emotionally calm
• breathable
• softly composed
• visually quiet
• premium through restraint

Whitespace should feel:
• intentional
• calming
• balanced

NOT:
❌ empty
❌ excessive
❌ mechanically spaced

RULE:
When uncertain, REMOVE rather than ADD.

-----------------------------------------------------

AVOID:
❌ helper text overload
❌ excessive labels
❌ decorative UI
❌ stacked chips everywhere
❌ loud visual hierarchy
❌ dense forms
❌ visible configuration systems
❌ excessive segmentation

-----------------------------------------------------

FAVOR:
✅ compressed interactions
✅ hidden complexity
✅ placeholders over explanations
✅ progressive disclosure
✅ natural language
✅ calm layouts
✅ emotionally invisible guidance

-----------------------------------------------------
✍️ UX WRITING PHILOSOPHY
-----------------------------------------------------

Pawple copy should be:
• short
• human
• obvious
• emotionally quiet
• natural

Avoid:
❌ long labels
❌ UX-writer-heavy phrasing
❌ explanatory helper text
❌ over-emotional narration
❌ instructional writing

Prefer:
✅ one-word labels
✅ compressed language
✅ example-driven placeholders

-----------------------------------------------------

GOOD:
“Meetup”
“Open to”
“Time”
“Joining paws”

BAD:
“What should nearby paws call this meetup?”
“Who’s this meetup best suited for?”
“When should nearby paws arrive?”

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
Placeholders should guide naturally.

Prefer:
examples over explanations.

-----------------------------------------------------
🔤 TYPOGRAPHY HIERARCHY (STRICT)
-----------------------------------------------------

PRIMARY FONT:
Inter

HANDWRITTEN FONT:
Caveat

-----------------------------------------------------

Inter is used for:
• UI
• buttons
• labels
• inputs
• metadata
• navigation
• settings
• legal text
• meetup UI
• onboarding
• tabs

-----------------------------------------------------

Caveat is ONLY used for:
• handwritten captions
• moment/journal writing
• emotionally personal text

-----------------------------------------------------

NEVER use Caveat for:
❌ buttons
❌ navigation
❌ labels
❌ forms
❌ tabs
❌ metadata
❌ legal text

-----------------------------------------------------

FONT SIZES

BODY / INPUTS:
Inter Regular 16px

LABELS / METADATA:
Inter Medium 14px

BUTTONS:
Inter SemiBold 16px

CARD TITLES:
Inter SemiBold 18px

PAGE TITLES:
Inter SemiBold 30px

HANDWRITTEN CAPTIONS:
Caveat Regular 18–20px

SMALL METADATA:
Inter Regular 12px

BRANDING:
Inter Medium 11px

-----------------------------------------------------
🎨 COLOR SYSTEM (STRICT TOKEN USAGE)
-----------------------------------------------------

ALL colors MUST come from:
theme.colors.*

NEVER hardcode colors except explicit brand colors below.

-----------------------------------------------------

BACKGROUND:
screen → #F5F4F1
card → #FBFAF8

-----------------------------------------------------

TEXT:
primary → #2F2F2F
secondary → #6A6A6A
muted → #7A7A7A
placeholder → #9A9A9A

-----------------------------------------------------

SAGE SYSTEM:
sage → #8FAF9B
sageLight → #E8F1EA
sageDark → #6D8B74

-----------------------------------------------------

HEART PURPLE:
#7B61FF

-----------------------------------------------------

FRAME COLOR:
#7A4F46

Alternative:
#70564B

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
Always import:
import { theme } from '../config/theme'

-----------------------------------------------------
📐 SPACING & SAFE AREA SYSTEM
-----------------------------------------------------

STRICT 8PT GRID ONLY:
8, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64

Avoid arbitrary spacing.

-----------------------------------------------------

SCREEN PADDING:
Top → 24px
Horizontal → 20px
Bottom → 32px

-----------------------------------------------------

SECTION GAP:
24px

-----------------------------------------------------

LABEL → INPUT GAP:
8px

-----------------------------------------------------

CARD PADDING:
16px

-----------------------------------------------------

BOTTOM SAFE AREA:
minimum 32px

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
Content must NEVER:
❌ collide with notch
❌ touch gesture area
❌ feel cramped vertically

-----------------------------------------------------

ALL screens MUST use:
SafeAreaView

-----------------------------------------------------

ScrollViews MUST use:
contentContainerStyle={{
  paddingTop: 24,
  paddingHorizontal: 20,
  paddingBottom: 32,
  flexGrow: 1,
}}

-----------------------------------------------------
🧩 COMPONENT SYSTEM
-----------------------------------------------------

BUTTONS:
• minHeight 48px
• borderRadius 22px
• Inter SemiBold 16px
• backgroundColor: theme.colors.sage

-----------------------------------------------------

INPUTS:
• borderRadius 16px
• minHeight 48px
• paddingVertical 14px
• paddingHorizontal 16px
• backgroundColor: theme.colors.background.card
• Inter Regular 16px

-----------------------------------------------------

CARDS:
• borderRadius 22px
• backgroundColor: theme.colors.background.card
• subtle shadow only
• marginBottom 24px

-----------------------------------------------------

BOTTOM SHEETS:
• soft appearance only
• handle width 40px
• handle height 4px
• radius 2px
• backdrop rgba(0,0,0,0.35)

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
Never use default React Native styling.

Everything must feel:
• soft
• calm
• premium
• restrained

-----------------------------------------------------
🖼️ FEED IMAGE & FRAME PHILOSOPHY
-----------------------------------------------------

Moment posts should feel like:
“printed memories softly placed on paper.”

NOT:
❌ image assets with overlays
❌ scrapbook templates
❌ graphic-designed cards

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
The frame ALWAYS exists OUTSIDE the image.

NEVER place:
❌ sketch lines
❌ doodles
❌ borders
❌ decorative overlays

INSIDE the photograph.

-----------------------------------------------------

FRAME RULES:
• warm maroon-brown only
• subtle imperfection
• slightly hand-drawn
• 2px max stroke
• ~75% opacity

-----------------------------------------------------

TILT RULES:
ONLY:
• image
• outer frame

may tilt.

-----------------------------------------------------

NEVER tilt:
❌ captions
❌ metadata
❌ branding
❌ card container

-----------------------------------------------------

ALL posts MUST maintain:
the SAME orientation direction.

Tilt:
-1.5deg maximum.

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
The pet/photo is ALWAYS the emotional focus.

The frame should support the memory quietly,
NOT dominate visually.

-----------------------------------------------------
📸 FEED CARD COMPOSITION
-----------------------------------------------------

Feed cards should feel:
• breathable
• calm
• handcrafted
• emotionally restrained

-----------------------------------------------------

IMAGE RATIO:
4:5 portrait

-----------------------------------------------------

IMAGE DOMINANCE:
~82% of card height

-----------------------------------------------------

BOTTOM CONTENT ORDER:
1. handwritten caption
2. pet name
3. metadata
4. subtle pawple branding

-----------------------------------------------------

HEART & SHARE:
• always OUTSIDE the card
• no counts
• no comments
• no reposts
• no social metrics

-----------------------------------------------------

HEART INTERACTION:
• pulse twice on first like
• fill purple
• remain purple until unliked

Animation:
soft only.
180–260ms.

-----------------------------------------------------

PAWPLE BRANDING:
• lowercase only
• subtle
• bottom-right
• never watermark-like

-----------------------------------------------------
🚫 ANTI-CLUTTER ENFORCEMENT
-----------------------------------------------------

Always minimize visible UI.

Hide complexity whenever possible.

Prefer:
• bottom sheets
• progressive disclosure
• collapsed interactions
• compressed UI

-----------------------------------------------------

Avoid:
❌ always-visible options
❌ giant forms
❌ helper paragraphs
❌ excessive chips
❌ configuration-heavy screens
❌ visual noise

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
If the same idea is already communicated naturally,
DO NOT create additional UI for it.

-----------------------------------------------------
🗄️ SUPABASE & DATA
-----------------------------------------------------

Always wrap DB calls in try/catch.

Log exact Supabase errors:
console.error('[Supabase]', error)

-----------------------------------------------------

Any displayed count or statistic (for example, Hosted or Participated meetups)
MUST be derived live from canonical junction tables using head/count queries:
select('id', { count: 'exact', head: true })

NEVER hardcode or cache stale counts.

-----------------------------------------------------

Always fetch:
supabase.auth.getUser()

before write operations.

-----------------------------------------------------

RULE:
Never modify:
❌ schemas
❌ RLS
❌ queries
❌ insert/update logic

unless explicitly instructed.

-----------------------------------------------------
🧠 STATE & CONTEXT
-----------------------------------------------------

The active pet is ALWAYS read from ActivePetContext.
NEVER read it from props, route params, or local guesses.

-----------------------------------------------------
🤖 AI OUTPUT BEHAVIOR
-----------------------------------------------------

ALWAYS:
• output complete runnable files
• preserve architecture
• preserve navigation
• preserve Supabase logic
• preserve state management

-----------------------------------------------------

WHEN MODIFYING UI:
Only change:
• styling
• spacing
• composition
• visual hierarchy

DO NOT break:
• logic
• data flow
• interactions

-----------------------------------------------------

ADD:
helpful beginner-friendly comments explaining WHY.

-----------------------------------------------------

MENTALLY TEST:
• imports
• theme mapping
• spacing
• safe areas
• prop usage
• navigation

before outputting.

-----------------------------------------------------
🚫 STRICT PROHIBITIONS
-----------------------------------------------------

❌ hardcoded colors
❌ hardcoded fonts
❌ arbitrary spacing
❌ Caveat outside emotional text
❌ visual clutter
❌ helper text overload
❌ dense layouts
❌ loud gradients
❌ strong shadows
❌ engagement metrics
❌ comments
❌ follower systems
❌ popularity systems
❌ overlapping safe areas
❌ navigation rewrites
❌ deleting architecture without instruction
❌ partial code outputs
❌ over-designed scrapbook aesthetics

-----------------------------------------------------
FINAL PRINCIPLE
-----------------------------------------------------

Pawple should feel:
like a calm emotional product,
not a designed interface.

TECH STACK: Expo SDK 51+ | React Native 0.74+ | React Navigation 6+ | Supabase JS v2 | react-native-safe-area-context
HEART ANIMATION: Use simple state-driven scale transform (Animated API). Pulse twice on first like. Duration: 200ms. No external libraries required.

FRAME IMPLEMENTATION: Use a styled View with subtle border-radius variation or a lightweight SVG path. Do NOT use image overlays, heavy shaders, or third-party frame packages.

When uncertain:
REMOVE rather than ADD.

-----------------------------------------------------
🆕 MEETUP & PROFILE DESIGN SYSTEM (LATEST)
-----------------------------------------------------
These rules apply specifically to the Meetup Cards, Pet Profile Hero, and My Meetups sections. They override general component rules where there is a conflict.

MEETUP CARD COLORS:
- Card Background: #FFFCF8
- Card Border: #F1E8DF
- Title Color: #6E8E73 (Sage Green variant for Meetup Titles ONLY)
- Primary Button: #9EB8A0 (Sage Green)
- Muted Accent (Labels/Icons): #8EA88F
- Date/Time Text: #4A403B
- Participant Text: #6B625C

MEETUP TYPOGRAPHY OVERRIDES:
- Meetup Card Title: Inter SemiBold 22px (Overrides general Card Title 18px)
- "YOUR MEETUP" Label: Inter Medium 11px, Letter Spacing 1px, Uppercase, #8EA88F
- Date & Time: Inter Medium 16px, #4A403B
- Location/Distance: Inter Regular 14px, #8EA88F

PET PROFILE HERO OVERRIDES:
- Pet Name: Inter SemiBold 26-28px, #3A312E
- Pet Subtitle (Breed • Age): Inter Medium 15px, #666
- Bio: Italicized, #888, Max 100 chars.
- Companion Badge: #9EB8A0 background, White text, rounded pill.

MEETUP ARCHITECTURE RULES:
- Meetups belong to PETS, not users. 
- Always use `meetup_hosts` and `meetup_participants` junction tables.
- Never show owner/human names on meetup cards. Only show pet names (e.g., "Hosted by Tyson • Peter").
- Mock data must always include at least 1 mock host pet. Participant count must be realistic (Hosts + User + Random Extras). Minimum count is 2.

STRICT MEETUP UI PROHIBITIONS:
- NO system emojis (like 📍) in the location line. Use clean text.
- NO fake "initial" avatars for hosts. Use real photos or just text names.
- NO double paw emojis. Use a single quiet paw or just text.
- NO heavy borders around sections. Use whitespace (24px) to separate.
- NO exclamation marks in the primary button ("You're Going", not "You're Going!").